<!--CLI Documentation — Introduction
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation.Introduction-->
<clidocumentation:Introduction xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:clicap="org.blockml.bml.cli.capability"
  xmlns:clidocumentation="org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Purpose and scope of the BlockML CLI
  </is>
  <documentation>
    The @blockml/cli package (blockml command) is the universal Node.js toolchain CLI.
    It wraps @blockml/compiler and @blockml/framework with file-system operations:
    config loading, TypeRegistry bootstrap, target bootstrap, compile/validate orchestration,
    and writing RenderOutput to disk.
    
    This library (org.blockml.bml.cli.*) is the SSOT. TypeScript in packages/cli-tools/src/
    implements it. Tests in packages/cli-tools/test/ encode behavioral contracts.
    
    V1 implements validate, compile, search, scan, graph, inspect, transform, and new (blockdoc, xsd, fatblock targets).
    Domain products use thin host CLIs (e.g. @machineblocks/cli) — see DualCliModel.
    
    Pipeline: loadConfig → bootstrapTypeRegistry → bootstrapTargets → compileToOutput → writeOutputFiles.
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidocumentation:LayerSeparation" relation="ReadNext" />
    <see type="clicap:RunCli" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
</clidocumentation:Introduction>
